# Local development: points at the Azurite emulator (run `npm run azurite` in another
# terminal). This is Azurite's well-known, publicly-documented dev storage account key —
# NOT a secret, safe to keep in this example file.
AZURE_STORAGE_CONNECTION_STRING="DefaultEndpointsProtocol=http;AccountName=devstoreaccount1;AccountKey=Eby8vdM02xNOcqFlqUwJPLlmEtlCDXJ1OUzFT50uSRZ6IFsuFq2UVErCz4I6tq/K1SZFPTOtr/KBHBeksoGMGw==;TableEndpoint=http://127.0.0.1:10002/devstoreaccount1;BlobEndpoint=http://127.0.0.1:10000/devstoreaccount1;"

# Signs the login session JWT (see lib/auth/session.ts). This example value is
# fine for local dev only — generate a fresh one for production
# (`openssl rand -base64 32`) and set it as a real secret on whatever hosts
# the app; never commit a production value.
AUTH_SECRET="z6QIAvWcUpYdpiq2xEDjUBSRsJA5wZmGuyQr3ydaZWk="

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Production, Option A (recommended if the subscription's free tier is free —
# confirm with SA first): Azure Cosmos DB, Table API, Free Tier ($0 forever,
# one per subscription). Same variable name, same SDK — no code change needed,
# just swap this value once provisioned. Shape (get the real one from Azure
# Portal → Cosmos DB account → "Connection String" blade):
#
#   AZURE_STORAGE_CONNECTION_STRING="DefaultEndpointsProtocol=https;AccountName=<cosmos-account-name>;AccountKey=<primary-key>;TableEndpoint=https://<cosmos-account-name>.table.cosmos.azure.com:443/;"
#
# See ../web/README.md "Cosmos DB Free Tier" section for the exact provisioning
# steps and the once-per-subscription caveat. NOT yet verified against a real
# Cosmos DB endpoint — re-run the verification steps there once you have one.

# Production, Option B: a real Azure Storage Account connection string (what
# this app was originally verified against) — always available, small ongoing
# cost (~$0.05/GB + tiny per-transaction fees, not free but close to it).
#
#   AZURE_STORAGE_CONNECTION_STRING="DefaultEndpointsProtocol=https;AccountName=<storage-account-name>;AccountKey=<primary-key>;TableEndpoint=https://<storage-account-name>.table.core.windows.net/;BlobEndpoint=https://<storage-account-name>.blob.core.windows.net/;"
#
# (Or, better than either raw connection string above: use Azure Static Web
# Apps' managed identity / Key Vault reference once that's provisioned, so no
# secret sits in an env var at all.)
